## Stakeholder Briefing

A simulated cybersecurity incident was conducted to evaluate the organization’s ability to detect and respond to threats. During the exercise, an attacker successfully exploited a vulnerable service and gained unauthorized administrative access to a system. Although direct detection on the target system was limited, suspicious activity was identified through monitoring tools and visualized using security dashboards. The response team was able to analyze the situation, document the incident, and block the attacker’s access.

Key performance metrics showed moderate detection and response times, indicating that the security operations are functional but can be improved. The exercise also included adversary emulation to simulate realistic attack behavior and validate monitoring capabilities.

The incident revealed gaps in system patching and monitoring coverage. It is recommended to improve system updates, enhance monitoring visibility, and implement automated response actions. Overall, the organization demonstrated effective incident handling, with opportunities to strengthen its defenses against future threats.